  "final_span": "data that isn\u2019t available in other ways. We aim to allow communities to take charge of generating data for their countries and regions, in addition to any governments willing to share their public health data.\nWithin a short time frame, it appears that each country encounters distinct challenges based on their respective stages of addressing air pollution. Hong Kong is at an advanced stage of recovery, akin to NGOs assisting in the cleanup. In the Philippines, we faced both floods and a significant impact\u2014infant mortality related to asthma in young babies. Yet it remains a new country, just beginning to learn about itself. Not even mapped out, it\u2019s bound to face air pollution problems. Every country is at a different stage, I believe.\nFor countries that aren\u2019t yet in a stage, we expect the government to make a data portal so",
